# Date words that alone take a more frequent non-date sense. A preposition,
# article, number or year beside the word keeps the date sense.
# August: male first name, and "dummer August", the clown (Duden "August",
# Vorname; Duden "August, der", Clown). The month takes a preposition, a day
# number or a year: "im August", "am 3. August", "August 2020".
august
